const postContent = "<p>Updated and source-checked: <strong>16 November 2026</strong>. The original publication date is retained above.</p>\n<h2>Start With When You Earned The Income</h2>\n<p>A calculator can show a plausible number using the wrong year's rules. In Pakistan, the normal Tax Year 2027 corresponds to <strong>1 July 2026 through 30 June 2027</strong>, or FY 2026–27. TY 2026 corresponds to the preceding financial year.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"/tools/tax-calculator\">Rafiqy Salary Tax Calculator</a> defaults to TY 2027 and keeps TY 2026 as a historical option. Choose the earning period before entering income. Do not use the year in which you happen to prepare a return as a substitute for the income period.</p>\n<h2>Salary Slabs For FY 2026–27</h2>\n<p>The following salary table is set out in FBR Circular 02 of 2026–27, dated 8 September 2026, page 4, item 7:</p>\n<table><thead><tr><th>Annual taxable salary (PKR)</th><th>Base income tax (PKR)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Up to 600,000</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Above 600,000 to 1,200,000</td><td>1% of the amount above 600,000</td></tr><tr><td>Above 1,200,000 to 2,200,000</td><td>6,000 + 11% above 1,200,000</td></tr><tr><td>Above 2,200,000 to 3,200,000</td><td>116,000 + 20% above 2,200,000</td></tr><tr><td>Above 3,200,000 to 4,100,000</td><td>316,000 + 25% above 3,200,000</td></tr><tr><td>Above 4,100,000 to 5,600,000</td><td>541,000 + 29% above 4,100,000</td></tr><tr><td>Above 5,600,000 to 7,000,000</td><td>976,000 + 32% above 5,600,000</td></tr><tr><td>Above 7,000,000</td><td>1,424,000 + 35% above 7,000,000</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p>Item 8 of the same circular explains that Finance Act 2026 withdrew the <strong>9% surcharge for salaried individuals</strong>. It does not remove the surcharge for other individuals and associations of persons.</p>\n<p>Official source: <a href=\"https://download1.fbr.gov.pk/Docs/202698139527880CircularNo.2of2026-27.pdf\">FBR Circular 02 of 2026–27</a>. The applicable law takes precedence over any calculator or summary.</p>\n<h2>A Raise Does Not Reprice Your Entire Salary</h2>\n<p>The marginal percentage applies to income above the threshold in its row. It does not apply to every rupee you earned.</p>\n<p>For an illustrative annual taxable salary of PKR 3,000,000, the TY 2027 calculation is PKR 116,000 plus 20% of PKR 800,000, giving PKR 276,000 before credits and adjustments. Dividing by 12 gives a planning average of PKR 23,000 per month.</p>\n<p>The calculator shows its threshold, fixed amount, marginal rate and surcharge separately so you can check the arithmetic. Fractional amounts immediately above a slab boundary remain taxable under the next slab rather than falling into a gap.</p>\n<h2>Bonuses And Monthly Deductions Need Care</h2>\n<p>Enter monthly taxable salary for a steady twelve-month scenario, then enter an additional annual taxable bonus separately. If a bonus is already included in the monthly figure, adding it again overstates income.</p>\n<p>The monthly figure is annual estimated tax divided by twelve. Payroll may withhold a different amount after a bonus, a job change, earlier deductions or an adjustment. Likewise, the average after-tax income spreads the annual bonus across twelve months; it is not a promise about the cash in a particular payslip.</p>\n<p>For variable salary or a partial employment year, first reconcile actual taxable annual amounts with payroll rather than blindly multiplying one payslip by twelve.</p>\n<h2>Keep Historical Rules And Personal Credits Separate</h2>\n<p>TY 2026 retains its own table and the historical 9% salary surcharge above PKR 10 million annual taxable income. The calculator's comparison uses identical income under both years' rules; it does not know your actual prior-year earnings.</p>\n<p>Historical source: <a href=\"https://download1.fbr.gov.pk/Docs/2025881983148210Income-Tax-Ordinance%2C-2001-Amended-upto-31.07.2025.pdf\">FBR Income Tax Ordinance, amended to 31 July 2025</a>, salary table and section 4AB.</p>\n<p>The current calculator deliberately reports tax <strong>before personal credits and rebates</strong>. It does not apply pension, donation, senior or teacher concessions simply because a checkbox was selected. Eligibility and supporting evidence need their own year-specific assessment.</p>\n<p>This version covers salary-only scenarios up to PKR 100 million annual taxable income. Mixed income, freelance/business income, special regimes, higher-income cases, withholding adjustments and other payroll deductions are outside its scope. Use a qualified adviser for those cases.</p>\n<h2>Check Without Uploading A Payslip</h2>\n<p>The tool accepts numbers and calculates in page memory. It does not require your name, CNIC, payslip, employer credentials or tax return, and it does not save salary entries to a database.</p>\n<p><a href=\"/tools/tax-calculator\">Open the Salary Tax Calculator</a> and choose the correct income period first.</p>"

